 "title": "Washington's Historic Georgetown Car Barn",
 "cat": "history",
 "emoji": "🚋",
 "sentences": [
  "Meet the Georgetown Car Barn!",
  "It was built between 1895 and 1897 by the Capital Traction Company.",
  "The architect Waddy Butler Wood designed it as a union terminal for streetcar lines.",
  "It even served as the terminal for Washington's only cable car system.",
  "Capital Traction converted the lines to electrical power almost immediately after it opened.",
  "The building housed streetcars until 1950 before changing ownership."
